# Python
backend/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Credentials. docker-compose interpolates from a repo-root .env, and README
# and backend/docs/spec.md both tell you to put real endpoint credentials there — so it
# must never be committable. `.env.example` stays tracked as the reference.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backend/.env

# Node / frontend
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/.pnpm-store/
# The frontend is pnpm-only: every image and compose service installs with
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, and pnpm-lock.yaml is the lockfile they
# read. A package-lock.json left behind by an `npm install` is installed from
# by nothing, but it makes `npm install` look like the supported way to add a
# dependency — and then package.json changes, the npm lockfile changes, and the
# lockfile the build actually uses does not. Ignored so it cannot be committed
# again; `src/lockfile_contract.test.js` catches the divergence itself.
frontend/package-lock.json

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.log

# CA bundles for internal endpoints — environment-specific, see
# backend/certs/README.md
backend/certs/*
!backend/certs/README.md
